# Packages baked into the live/install environment itself -- deliberately
# thin: just what the installer needs to run. The install itself is fully
# offline (D-0063/D-0064): the whole packages/*.txt closure is baked into a
# local repo (iso/build-offline-repo) that pacstrap reads, and the repo itself
# is baked in at /root/autarchy, so none of that is listed here. No AUR
# packages here -- archiso can't build them, and this project doesn't run a
# custom repo/mirror to work around that (D-0050).
#
# One bare package name per line: mkarchiso reads this file directly (not
# through scripts/pkglist), and only understands whole-line '#' comments --
# no trailing inline comments, unlike this project's own packages/*.txt
# convention. Found the hard way: a trailing inline comment on a package
# line becomes part of the package name, and mkarchiso fails with
# "target not found: <name><trailing whitespace>".

# Boot-critical: without these the ISO doesn't boot as a live environment at all.
base
linux
linux-firmware
mkinitcpio
mkinitcpio-archiso
# microcode; hardware unknown until first boot (base-install.md step 2)
intel-ucode
amd-ucode

# Disk layout tools (base-install.md steps 4-5: partition, LUKS, Btrfs, ESP)
# sgdisk
gptfdisk
# partprobe -- install-base-system calls it right after sgdisk; missing
# here on a real hardware boot test ("partprobe: command not found"),
# unlike the stock Arch ISO, which carries it by default
parted
cryptsetup
btrfs-progs
# mkfs.fat for the ESP
dosfstools
# pacstrap, genfstab, arch-chroot
arch-install-scripts
efibootmgr

# Network (Phase 17): NetworkManager, the same stack the installed system runs
# (D-0014), for wired and wireless. Install needs no network at all, but a
# Wi-Fi connection made here -- in the installer's Wi-Fi page, or with nmtui from
# a shell -- is carried to the new system as a plain NetworkManager connection
# file. It brings its own DHCP client and wpa_supplicant; iwd and dhcpcd are
# deliberately absent, a second manager would fight it for the interface.
networkmanager
systemd-resolvconf
# Diagnosing hardware from the live session (Phase 17): why Wi-Fi is blocked or
# missing. iw for the regulatory domain and the adapter, lspci/lsusb to see whether
# the adapter is there at all, evtest to see whether a hotkey (a laptop's Wi-Fi
# key) sends the OS an event.
iw
pciutils
usbutils
evtest

# Repo access (replaces today's manual `pacman -Sy git github-cli` -- runbook
# step 1) and the test runner for the Red step (runbook step 3).
git
github-cli
bats
bats-assert
bats-support

# Editing the vars file (base-install.md step 1: `vim base-install.local.vars`)
# and a usable text console.
vim
tmux
sudo

# The real guided installer (Phase 15): a hand-written GTK4/libadwaita
# app, kiosk-launched via cage on tty1 (.bash_profile). No vulkan-intel
# here -- GSK_RENDERER is pinned to the GL renderer (.bash_profile),
# deliberately not the Vulkan one GTK defaults to, so the live
# environment doesn't need a Vulkan driver at all.
cage
gtk4
libadwaita
python-gobject
mesa
adwaita-icon-theme
cantarell-fonts
